  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When two players with avatars that have seats on them try to sit on each other at the same time, it causes both avatars to start going haywire. Every time it happened we ended up falling out of the world. It'd likely something to do with the motion data that would normally make the sitting avatar track along with the avatar with the seat, but since both are sitting on each other, it's trying to use both sets of motion data which keeps stacking on itself causing the avatars to bug out.",
